cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GlucoTrace in research, please cite it as below."
title: "GlucoTrace: a small, pre-registered representation encoder for continuous glucose monitor data"
version: 0.3.1
date-released: 2026-10-05
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22935995
repository-code: "https://github.com/Aman-Tripathi27/GlucoTrace"
url: "https://aman-tripathi27.github.io/GlucoTrace/"
authors:
  - family-names: Tripathi
    given-names: Aman
keywords:
  - continuous glucose monitoring
  - representation learning
  - time series
  - transformer
abstract: >-
  GlucoTrace encodes a 24-hour CGM day into a 128-number fingerprint with a
  compact mask-aware Transformer. Missing readings are never interpolated,
  splits are participant-disjoint and checksummed, and every release decision
  follows an evaluation protocol declared before training. Research use only;
  not a medical device.
